    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cēnācŭlārĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caen-</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coen-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		cenaculum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pertaining to a garret;</i> only twice <i>subst.</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cēnācŭlā-rĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a tenant of a
				garret</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 13, 7, 11, §
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cēnācŭlārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a leasing of a
				garret</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exercere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 9, 3, 5, § 1</span></i>
			.</div>
